# Normalise line endings to LF in the working tree, not just in the repository.
#
# This matters concretely: the container entrypoint is a shell script, and a CRLF
# checkout on Windows turns its shebang into "#!/bin/sh\r", which Linux reports as a
# missing interpreter. Pinning LF keeps a Windows clone able to build the image.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.mako text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
